# Force LF for everything text-based, regardless of which OS commits it. Found the hard way:
# a CRLF line ending inside a YAML `run:` block's single-quoted bash string breaks quote-parsing
# on the ubuntu-latest Actions runner ("unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''"), even
# though the same content runs fine locally. CN-07 already flags cross-platform risk generally;
# this is the CI/tooling half of that, not the application-runtime half.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db binary
